-- R3's per-root check (IMPLICIT-PROPS-DESIGN.md §11.4). One binder per name PER
-- ROOT: two sibling sections may each declare `foo`, and each is read by its own
-- subtree, but a single directive or @export that reaches both ends up with two
-- inputs spelled `foo` and no way to say which one a value is for.
--
-- `both` reads section 1's `foo` directly and section 2's through `g`. The
-- measured swing this catches: with these two lines under section 1 the answer
-- is 991 -- the supply reached one `foo`, and the other fell back to its own
-- default of 99 -- while under section 2 the identical lines give 11. `l4 check`
-- used to succeed both times.
--
-- The remedy is R3's three. Bridging at the call is the one that keeps both
-- sections: `foo PLUS (g WITH foo IS foo)` takes section 2's binder off this
-- root's read-set by the §2.2 subtraction and leaves one.

§ `1`
    GIVEN foo IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 4

GIVETH A NUMBER
`both` MEANS foo PLUS g

#EVAL `both` WITH foo IS 1

§ `2`
    GIVEN foo IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 99

GIVETH A NUMBER
g MEANS foo TIMES 10
